{
  "id": "04-kth-largest-element-in-array",
  "title": "Kth Largest Element in an Array",
  "track": "Hash Maps",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "topics": [
    "hash-maps",
    "selection"
  ],
  "source": "canonical Kth Largest Element in an Array concept; description, examples, and tests re-authored",
  "description": "The input is an array of integers nums and an integer k. Return the k-th largest value in the array, counting duplicates: with nums = [7, 9, 7, 4, 6] and k = 3 the sorted order is 9, 7, 7, 6, 4, so the answer is 7.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= k <= len(nums) <= 5000",
    "-10000 <= nums[i] <= 10000"
  ],
  "parameters": [
    "nums",
    "k"
  ],
  "functionName": "kth_largest",
  "starterCode": "def kth_largest(nums, k):\n    # Return the k-th largest value, counting duplicates.\n    ...\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": {
        "nums": [
          7,
          9,
          7,
          4,
          6
        ],
        "k": 3
      },
      "output": 7,
      "explanation": "Sorted descending: 9, 7, 7, 6, 4. The third value is 7."
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "nums": [
          5,
          1
        ],
        "k": 2
      },
      "output": 1,
      "explanation": "The 2nd largest of two values is the smaller one."
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "If the array were sorted, which single position would you read?",
    "Sorting everything is more work than needed. A structure that keeps only the k biggest values seen so far is enough.",
    "Sort descending and read index k - 1 for O(n log n); or keep a min-heap of size k and return its root for O(n log k); quickselect reaches O(n) on average."
  ],
  "solution": "Sort the array in descending order and return the value at index k - 1: O(n log n) time, O(n) space for the sorted copy. A size-k min-heap brings this to O(n log k) time, and quickselect to O(n) average time; the sort is the reference answer here.",
  "solutionCode": "def kth_largest(nums, k):\n    return sorted(nums, reverse=True)[k - 1]\n",
  "bruteForceCode": "def kth_largest(nums, k):\n    remaining = list(nums)\n    for _ in range(k - 1):\n        biggest = 0\n        for i in range(1, len(remaining)):\n            if remaining[i] > remaining[biggest]:\n                biggest = i\n        remaining.pop(biggest)\n    biggest = 0\n    for i in range(1, len(remaining)):\n        if remaining[i] > remaining[biggest]:\n            biggest = i\n    return remaining[biggest]\n",
  "failureHint": "hidden tests include duplicates of the answer, k = 1, k = len(nums), and negative values",
  "expectedComplexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
